{
  "name": "498. An operator lists and releases output folder claims, and a key with no storage list does not claim a bucket root (storage folder claims) [SERIAL]",
  "description": "TXE-7259. Local fixture regression, no live provider call: run with providerErrorFixture=1 against the gateway of tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json, with tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs as the only upstream. Since TXE-7121 (folder 497) a virtual key claims the output folder it first writes into, and no request releases a claim. Three things change here. A key with no allowed_storage_prefixes that writes to the root of a bucket does not claim the bucket (498.3 to 498.5): one request would otherwise take the whole bucket from every other key. An operator lists claims with GET /api/governance/storage-folders and releases one with DELETE /api/governance/storage-folders?folder=<uri> (498.6 to 498.12): after the release the next key to write there claims the folder. A batch whose create named no output folder (as one created before folders were claimed) has the output directory its retrieve names claimed for its creator (498.13 to 498.16): the fixture batch created with metadata.fixture_output_dir retrieves as completed with that directory as output_file_id, and another key then cannot read a result file in it. A deleted key keeps its claims until an operator releases them (498.17 to 498.19), since dropping them would hand the folder contents to every key with no storage list. 498.20 pins that only the five served batch creates reached the provider. The folder and bucket names carry a per-run suffix because a claim outlives the key that made it; 498.21 and 498.22 release the two claims the run leaves.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "498.1 [setup] virtual key A",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "  return;",
              "}",
              "pm.collectionVariables.unset('claimVkA'); pm.collectionVariables.unset('claimVkAId'); pm.collectionVariables.unset('claimVkB'); pm.collectionVariables.unset('claimVkBId');",
              "pm.sendRequest({ url: pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixtureUrl') + '/__reset', method: 'POST' }, function (err, res) {",
              "  pm.test('the fixture was reset', function () { pm.expect(err, String(err)).to.equal(null); pm.expect(res.code).to.equal(200); });",
              "});",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('claimRun', String(Date.now()) + '-' + Math.floor(Math.random() * 1000000));"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('the virtual key was created', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.code, pm.response.text()).to.equal(200); });",
              "var created = (pm.response.json() || {}).virtual_key || {};",
              "pm.test('it has an id and a value', function () { pm.expect(created.id, pm.response.text()).to.be.a('string').and.not.equal(''); pm.expect(created.value, pm.response.text()).to.be.a('string').and.not.equal(''); });",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('claimVkA', created.value || ''); pm.collectionVariables.set('claimVkAId', created.id || '');"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"name\":\"harness-498-a-{{$guid}}\",\"provider_configs\":[{\"provider\":\"storage_uri_files\",\"weight\":1,\"allowed_models\":[\"*\"],\"key_ids\":[\"*\"]}]}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
